    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113158" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκό-πῠλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with gates of brass</i>
			or <i>bronze,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱρόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.181
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. θεά,</span> epith. of Athena,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				1113
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ,</span> of Castalia,
			because issuing <i>from bronze spouts</i> in the shape of lions'
			heads, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Pae.</u>
				6.7
			</span></i>.</div>
